{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Aaron took — each his fire-pan.</b> They reasoned that just as after the daily burnt-offering, upon which the Shekhinah rests — as it says: עֹלַת תָּמִיד לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם פֶּתַח אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד לִפְנֵי ה׳, אֲשֶׁר אִוָּעֵד לָכֶם שָׁמָּה (Exodus 29:42) — the incense would follow, so too it was fitting to offer new incense now, upon the revelation of the glory of YHWH to all the people and upon the descent of the fire. Therefore they offered it." "<b>Before YHWH.</b> On the inner altar, concerning which it says: וְלֹא תַעֲלוּ עָלָיו קְטֹרֶת זָרָה (Exodus 30:9). And even if it would have been fitting to do so had they been commanded in this matter, they sinned by doing so now." "<b>Which He had not commanded them.</b> As they, of blessed memory, stated (Eiruvin 63a): they issued a halakhic ruling in the presence of Moses their master."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The quoted verse reads אִוָּעֵד (Sforno's form) for the standard אִוָּעֵד; the sense is 'where I will meet with you.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:03.884419359Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}